==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|fliohan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fleuhaną}}. Cognate with Dutch {{m|nl|vlieden}} and English {{m|en|flee}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈfliː.ən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-fliehen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|flieht|floh|geflohen|auxiliary=both}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[flee]]; to [[escape]]
